                                   CH2PH NOTES

1. A lot of the unresolved #defines are unres because they involve casts.
See if the cast can be safely ignored, ie., ends up as an integer type.

On thinking about this, I see a lot of casts to unrepresentable objects
(like (char *) 5). What is casted is or is not going to be a constant, 
and it either is or is not going to be casted to a reasonable type.
If not, like the char * case, then there is nothing we can do about it
anyways, so we can pass it and leave it to the programmer to deal with
it. Either way, this argues for ignoring the cast.

2. Some coined #define names (that appear in the report), don't appear
to be in any list.

3. Should see if a coined #define is actually going to be used (resolved)
before including it in the coin report. Unsed items make no sense to list
there.

4. Should we place the post macro-resolved string in the unresolved report,
instead of/in addition to, the source macro ?

5. Find out what text("....") means.

6. L"string" is a wide character string. Recognize and treat as a string
in macros.

7. "ch2ph" could theoretically be extended to "ctop" by storing the
intermediate graph of the program mesh encountered, and processing that.
This is mentioned here mainly because that would also help header translations.
Seeing how variables are actually used could help resolve declarations.
For example:

void myfunc(int *a)

{

    while (*a) a++;
    ...

}

Establishes "a" as an array reference, and not a var reference because the
pointer is used to walk past the first element of a. 
